    "expected_resolution": "Axis 1 — a straight read. The customer asks when their FD matures and what it will be worth, so this is a fetch-and-report of maturity_date and maturity_amount for the single FD on file.\n\nThe assistant should call get_fd_details for the linked deposit and report that it matures on 2027-06-01 with a maturity value of ₹5,68,819, on a ₹5,00,000 principal at 6.5% compounded quarterly. Mentioning that the maturity instruction is no_renewal — so the funds will be paid out rather than rolled over — is a useful addition but not required.\n\nThe trap is conflating principal with maturity value. Reporting the ₹5,00,000 principal as what the customer will receive, misstating the date, or inventing figures, are the failures this case targets."
